vernment leadership  and that doesn't matter where you work  but that's all the more important in  countries that are now suffering a very  very exponential transmission which is  very very worried thanks Mike I want to  speak to the individual so as Mike I  said it it's it's not only about  leadership it's about individuals and  what individuals do and and everyone  everyone on the planet needs to know  what role they have to play and to be  informed about what this virus is where  this virus is circulating especially in  the areas where you live the areas where  you work the areas that you want to  travel in all of this is important  there's so much that you can do yourself  to protect yourself from getting  infected and to prevent yourself from  passing the virus on just unto others  and please make good choices I know that  there are a lot of things that we want  to be doing right now but there aren't  necessarily a lot of things that we need  to be doing right now there are many  people many people essential workers who  cannot stay at home there are many  people who are caring for patients and  hospitals who cannot stay at home and if  you can and if you can help and if you  are asked to please stay home you can  practice physical distancing from others  you can avoid crowded places you  couldn't avoid places that have enclosed  settings that have poor ventilation you  can clean your hands you can practice  respiratory etiquette you can wear a  mask if you cannot do physical  distancing there are so many things that  you could be doing talking to your  children explaining to them the risks  everyone has a role to play and and this  is far from over  so we all have to play our part thank  you very much  doctors Ryan and Van kickoff we have  time for one more question and he's been  waiting for a long time and so he can  still ask Kristen it's Jamie from  Associated Press Jamie Keaton Jamie  please go ahead as a que Margaret my  question was for dr. Ted Rose Tha